# Git commit author

When creating git commits in this repo:

- **Author:** `Emmanuel Ombaye <Emmanuelombaye@users.noreply.github.com>`
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or commit as `cursoragent` / `James Sio`.
- Pass author explicitly (do not change global git config):

```bash
git commit --author="Emmanuel Ombaye <Emmanuelombaye@users.noreply.github.com>" -m "message"
```

Push to `origin main` after commits when the user asks to send changes to GitHub.
